			<!-- Isn't this just Marp? -->
			<section class="border-y border-border bg-muted py-[clamp(48px,6vw,88px)]">
				<div class="wrap">
					<SectionHead
						eyebrow="The fair question"
						title="“Isn’t Lattice just Marp with a coat of paint?”"
					>
						No. We did start from Marp’s one good idea — write the deck in Markdown, render it through headless
						Chromium to PDF — building on its engine early, then replacing it with our own at v1.0.0. Plain text buys
						a deck you can track and compare, true of every code engine; determinism is rarer — several print through
						the browser and drift from machine to machine. And Marp itself stays deliberately skinny: no component
						system, no design tokens, no layout primitives — a few generic themes and raw CSS, by design. Fair for a
						framework; it just isn’t a design system. Lattice brings the rest:
					</SectionHead>
					<div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-[26px] shadow-sm">
						<h3 class="m-0 mb-3 t-body text-[17px] font-semibold text-[var(--text-heading)]">What Lattice is now</h3>
						<ul class="m-0 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.55] text-foreground lg:columns-2 lg:gap-10 [&>li]:break-inside-avoid">
							<li><strong>More than fifty components</strong> across thirteen buckets. Pick the meaning, get the composition.</li>
							<li>A <strong>design-token system</strong> and <strong>14 editorial palettes + 4 color-blind-safe</strong>. Layouts never name a color.</li>
							<li><strong>Boardroom-grade defaults</strong> and WCAG-AA contrast in every palette, light and dark.</li>
							<li>An <strong>owned, pinned render engine</strong>. It renders plain HTML sections, not SVG-wrapped slides, so modern CSS works natively — container queries, counters, masks — and layout holds across browsers.</li>
							<li><strong>Agent authoring.</strong> A machine catalog and a shared linter give an LLM rails, so it composes valid, on-brand decks.</li>
							<li><strong>The Studio.</strong> The whole loop in a browser tab — write with live preview, get coached, apply fixes from chat, present — nothing to install.</li>
							<li><strong>A finish layer.</strong> Premium surface treatments — marks, washes, backdrops — applied with one line and tuned visually in Fabricate, the Studio’s finish designer.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

